<section class="by-hero"><div class="by-w by-hero-g"><div class="by-hero-t"><p class="by-scr by-hero-k">dawat-e-dastarkhwan</p><h1>Fragrant rice,<br>slow <span>dum</span>,<br>full table.</h1><p class="by-lead">Biryani is a warm home kitchen guide to the dish that turns dinner into a celebration. Plan a handi for your whole table, build a whole-spice blend by taste, and learn to seal and cook on dum like a patient cook.</p>
<div class="by-hero-a"><a class="by-btn" href="#batch">Plan my handi</a><a class="by-btn by-btn-o" href="#spice">Blend my spices</a></div></div>
<div class="by-hero-v"><figure class="by-arch"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1782541370275-6761522e39d1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=700&q=75" alt="hands serving chicken biryani with lemon" width="560" height="700" fetchpriority="high"></figure><figure class="by-round"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1752673508949-f4aeeaef75f0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=280&h=280&q=75" alt="a rice dish served in a clay bowl" width="280" height="280" fetchpriority="high"></figure><svg class="by-steam" viewBox="0 0 120 140" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 130c-16-22 16-34 0-58s16-34 0-58M60 130c-16-22 16-34 0-58s16-34 0-58M90 130c-16-22 16-34 0-58s16-34 0-58"/></svg><p class="by-seal">Dum<br><span>30 min</span></p></div></div></section>

<section class="by-ing"><div class="by-w"><div class="by-ing-h"><p class="by-scr">the three treasures</p><h2 class="rv">Small things that make a big biryani</h2></div><div class="by-ing-g"><article class="by-ig rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1760982686043-b58138aab8eb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=480&q=75" alt="purple saffron flowers with red stigmas" width="400" height="480" loading="lazy"></figure><b>Kesar</b><p>Saffron threads bloomed in warm milk, for colour and perfume.</p></article><article class="by-ig rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1763558049571-a6d12a85472e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=480&q=75" alt="green cardamom pods held in a hand" width="400" height="480" loading="lazy"></figure><b>Elaichi</b><p>Green cardamom: the sweet, floral heart of the spice blend.</p></article><article class="by-ig rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1528569051709-22528f7c7527?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=480&q=75" alt="a bowl of sliced onions" width="400" height="480" loading="lazy"></figure><b>Birista</b><p>Onions fried slowly to deep gold, for crunch and sweetness.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="by-s by-bt" id="batch"><div class="by-w by-bt-g"><div class="by-card"><p class="by-tag">Kitchen tool &middot; 1</p><h2 class="rv">Handi planner</h2><p class="by-p">Choose how many guests and which style you are cooking. We scale rice, meat or vegetables, yogurt, fried onions and ghee, and tell you how far to parboil the rice and how long to keep it on dum.</p>
<label class="by-lb" for="bt-g">Guests <b id="bt-gv">6</b></label><input type="range" id="bt-g" min="2" max="30" value="6" class="by-rng">
<p class="by-lb">Style</p><div class="by-chips" id="bt-s" role="group" aria-label="Style"><button type="button" class="on" data-v="0">Kacchi (raw marinated meat)</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Pakki (cooked gravy)</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Vegetable</button></div>
<p class="by-lb">Appetite</p><div class="by-chips" id="bt-a" role="group" aria-label="Appetite"><button type="button" data-v="0">Light, with sides</button><button type="button" class="on" data-v="1">Main event</button></div></div>
<div class="by-bt-r" aria-live="polite"><div class="by-handi"><div class="by-layers" id="bt-ly"></div></div><p class="by-handi-c"><b id="bt-r"></b>basmati rice for this handi</p><ul class="by-list" id="bt-l"></ul><p class="by-p by-note" id="bt-n"></p><div class="by-bt-i"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1777726041709-7e2875bfa0e0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=220&q=75" alt="a close-up of fluffy white basmati rice grains" width="300" height="220" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1780656521144-548577a6e6c8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=220&q=75" alt="a spoon full of uncooked rice" width="300" height="220" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></div></section>

<section class="by-s by-sp" id="spice"><div class="by-w by-sp-g"><div class="by-plate-w"><div class="by-plate" id="sp-plate" aria-hidden="true"></div><figure class="by-sp-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1783309240074-24cebbeb81a9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=240&q=75" alt="different spices in metal bowls" width="520" height="240" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<div><p class="by-tag by-tag-2">Kitchen tool &middot; 2</p><h2 class="rv">Whole spice blender</h2><p class="by-p">Biryani is perfumed with whole spices added to the rice water and the layers. Set how warm and how floral you like it, and the weight of rice, and we suggest a balanced handful.</p>
<label class="by-lb" for="sp-r">Uncooked rice <b id="sp-rv">500 g</b></label><input type="range" id="sp-r" min="250" max="2000" step="250" value="500" class="by-rng">
<label class="by-lb" for="sp-w">Warmth (clove, pepper, cinnamon) <b id="sp-wv">balanced</b></label><input type="range" id="sp-w" min="0" max="2" value="1" class="by-rng">
<label class="by-lb" for="sp-f">Fragrance (cardamom, mace, kewra) <b id="sp-fv">balanced</b></label><input type="range" id="sp-f" min="0" max="2" value="1" class="by-rng">
<ul class="by-sl" id="sp-l" aria-live="polite"></ul><p class="by-p by-note" id="sp-n"></p></div></div></section>

<section class="by-gd"><div class="by-w by-gd-g"><a class="by-gc rv" href="biryani-styles-guide.html"><span class="by-scr">guide one</span><b>Biryani Styles, Kacchi &amp; Pakki</b><p>How Hyderabadi, Lucknowi, Kolkata and other regional biryanis differ, and what kacchi and pakki mean.</p><em>Read the guide</em></a><a class="by-gc by-gc2 rv" href="dum-cooking-guide.html"><span class="by-scr">guide two</span><b>Cooking on Dum</b><p>Layering, sealing the pot and the gentle heat that lets rice and spice steam together.</p><em>Read the guide</em></a></div></section>

